A Class I, Division 1 rating is required for all electrical wiring (as well as electrical 
equipment) due to the expectation that a flammable atmosphere may be present at some time 
from operations. NFPA 70 Article 500-5 (National Electric Code)

Brainstorming is an activity where individuals generate ideas related to a topic or task; 
done in groups or individually with no restriction on quality of ideas. Once ideas are 
generated, they are then evaluated and a decision about which to pursue is made.
